  "text": "To find the sum of the \\( y \\)-coordinates of the intersection points between the parabola \\( x = 34y^2 \\) and the piecewise linear function \\( f(x) \\), we need to solve the equation \\( 34y^2 = f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the range \\([-1, 3)\\) and then find the corresponding \\( y \\)-coordinates.\n\nThe piecewise linear function is defined as:\n\\[ f(x) = \\begin{cases} x & \\text{if } x \\in [-1, 1) \\\\ 2 - x & \\text{if } x \\in [1, 3) \\end{cases} \\]\n\nWe need to consider the intersection points for \\( x \\in [-1, 1) \\) and \\( x \\in [1, 3) \\) separately.\n\n1. For \\( x \\in [-1, 1) \\):\n\\[ 34y^2 = x \\]\n\\[ y^2 = \\frac{x}{34} \\]\nSince \\( x \\in [-1, 1) \\), we have \\( y^2 \\in [0, \\frac{1}{34}) \\). The corresponding \\( y \\)-coordinates are \\( y = \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{34}} \\).\n\n2. For \\( x \\in [1, 3) \\):\n\\[ 34y^2 = 2 - x \\]\n\\[ y^2 = \\frac{2 - x}{34} \\]\nSince \\( x \\in [1, 3) \\), we have \\( y^2 \\in [0, \\frac{1}{17}) \\). The corresponding \\( y \\)-coordinates are \\( y = \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2 - x}{34}} \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of the \\( y \\)-coordinates. Since the function is periodic with period 4, we only need to consider the interval \\([-1, 3)\\).\n\nFor \\( x \\in [-1, 1) \\):\nThe sum of the \\( y \\)-coordinates is:\n\\[ 2 \\left( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{34}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{34}} \\right) = 2 \\left( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{34}} \\right) = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{34}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{34}}{34} = \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{17} \\]\n\nFor \\( x \\in [1, 3) \\):\nThe sum of the \\( y \\)-coordinates is:\n\\[ 2 \\left( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{17}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{17}} \\right) = 2 \\left( \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{17}} \\right) = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{17}}{17} \\]\n\nAdding these two sums together:\n\\[ \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{17} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{17}}{17} = \\frac{\\sqrt{34} + 2\\sqrt{17}}{17} \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the \\( y \\)-coordinates is \\( \\frac{2 + 2\\sqrt{34}}{17} \\). In the form \\( \\frac{a + b\\sqrt{c}}{d} \\), we have \\( a = 2 \\), \\( b = 2 \\), \\( c = 34 \\), and \\( d = 17 \\).\n\nSince \\( a, b, \\) and \\( d \\) have greatest common divisor equal to 1 and \\( c \\) is not divisible by the square of any prime, the final answer is:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = 2 + 2 + 34 + 17 = 55 \\]\n\nThe answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{55}\n\\]",
